🟡 **SUGGESTION: Guard `_revealedNow` with `hasContentDimensions`**

`ScrollPosition.maxScrollExtent` is implemented as `_maxScrollExtent!` in the framework — it **throws** if read after a client attaches but before `applyContentDimensions` runs:

```dart
bool get _revealedNow {
  if (!_chatScrollController.hasClients) return true;
  final position = _chatScrollController.position;
  return position.pixels >= position.maxScrollExtent - _topRevealSlack;
}
```

I traced the current call sites and the race is practically unreachable (build-phase reads see the previous frame's layout state; the post-frame callbacks and scroll listeners all run after layout), so this is not a live bug — but the guard is one property away from being structurally safe:

```dart
bool get _revealedNow {
  if (!_chatScrollController.hasClients) return true;
  final position = _chatScrollController.position;
  if (!position.hasContentDimensions) return true;
  return position.pixels >= position.maxScrollExtent - _topRevealSlack;
}
```

That keeps `_revealedNow` total for any future call site (it is a public-shaped getter already called from three different phases).

